  "notes": "\"Hats are the identity\" — the research's own words — so this model carries the densest hat stream in the batch: `base` fixed to `8T`, `continuous` true, `fillDensity` 0.72, against Jeezy's non-continuous 8ths at 0.32 at the far end of the same genre. The triplet is authored on the *base* rather than in the roll vocabulary, which is the honest place for it: the research describes a continuous triplet stream that the rolls shadow, not a stream of rolls. ⚠ **The roll frequency is capped at 0.20 by this batch's authoring band**, and the research asks for 32nd rolls that shadow the vocal triplets; what carries that here is the triplet base and the high fill density, not the roll count. Harmony is \"static i vamps and i–VI two-chord beds\" over \"sparse 3–6-pitch motifs, high register over a root-only low voice\": `motifPitchCount` 5 with `melody.register` [75, 97] and `maxChords` 2. \"Long enough decay to blur into the next hit\" is `sustain: legato` with `monoCutSelf` inherited, and \"short glides matching the melodic root\" is a `M2`/`m3`-weighted slide set rather than the octave. ⚠ **The counter is authored knowing it is the wrong instrument.** The research says the countermelody is \"usually a vocal ad-lib rather than an instrument\" and there is no ad-lib lane; `answer_lick` at the top weight with `densityRatio` 0.42 is a lick answering every second beat, which is the gesture the ad-lib performs. `confidence` is `high` — the flow has formal academic analysis and the production lineage is heavily documented. INFERRED: every velocity figure and the family weights; the occasional major-mode celebratory beat the research mentions is not modelled, because a second mode would be a second model. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
